On 8 September 2026, an ethical hacking investigation identified vulnerabilities in Adalat AI’s infrastructure. We worked with the researcher (
@ni5arga
) to investigate and patch

evidence.text:
On 8 September 2026, an ethical hacking investigation identified vulnerabilities in Adalat AI’s infrastructure. We worked with the researcher (
@ni5arga
) to investigate and patch them. No court-user data was accessed whatsoever.

Our joint write-up explains what happened, how AI agents were used to connect vulnerabilities, how we mitigated it, and how separating infrastructure access from document decryption helped protect user data.

As AI agents become more capable at finding and connecting vulnerabilities, we need to keep learning from the wider security community. We’ll be launching a vulnerability disclosure program to invite researchers to help us further strengthen our systems.

We’re sharing these lessons to help others in the ecosystem and build dependable technology that public institutions can trust for the long term.

Thanks to Nisarga Adhikary 
@ni5arga
 for his investigation and collaboration.

